  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R</p><p>Assertion A: In the Ellingham diagram, a sharp change in slope of the line is observed from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>MgO</mi></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><msup><mn>1120</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p><p>Reason R: There is a large change of entropy associated with the change of state</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mP6OZ",
      "text": "Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "feIft",
      "text": "A is false but R is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vMz4q",
      "text": "Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cH1f9",
      "text": "A is true but R is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0c8f366f-1659-49b0-bbc2-3d7def692ca7.png\" style=\"width: 253px; height: 235px;\" /></p><p>For line II&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>&nbsp;is more negative than line I.&nbsp;In the Ellingham diagram, a sharp change in slope of the line is observed for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>MgO</mi></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><msup><mn>1120</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;because that is the boiling point of magnesium.</p><p>From diagram, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>solid</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>solid</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>II</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>liquid</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>solid</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>There is a large increase in entropy associated with the change of state of magnesium.</p><p>So, both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).</p>",
    "image": null
  },
